On Saturday evening, I cook in the flat.
I sit down at the table and eat.
Bruno comes to me immediately.
He sits right next to my chair.
He looks at me.
His eyes are very big and sad.
I laugh.
But I have to stay strong.
Sabine's rules are important.
I look at him.
"Bruno, no," I say.
He whines a little.
"Go to your basket!" I say firmly.
He just stays sitting.
"Dogs are not allowed to eat human food," I explain.
Of course, he does not understand the words, but he understands my voice.
He slowly walks to his basket.
He lies down and sighs loudly.
I continue eating my dinner in peace.
